# Local env files. `.env.example` IS committed; real values never are.
#
# `.env` is listed explicitly and NOT just via `.env*.local`: a bare `.env` is the
# name people reach for by habit, `vercel dev` reads it too, and the old pattern let
# one straight through into a commit on 2026-08-04. The negation keeps the example
# file committed while everything else in the family is ignored.
#
# KEEP `!.env.example` LAST in this family. Later patterns win, so a broad `.env*`
# added anywhere below would silently re-ignore it -- which `vercel link` did on
# 2026-08-04, appending its own `.env*` to the end of this file. `.env.example` only
# stayed in the repo because it was already tracked. If the CLI adds that line again,
# delete it rather than leaving it after the negation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS. `.vscode/settings.json` and `.vscode/extensions.json` are
